cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "species2vec: distributed species embeddings that recover range overlap from GBIF co-occurrence"
authors:
  - family-names: Angelov
    given-names: Boyan
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/boyanangelov/species2vec"
url: "https://github.com/boyanangelov/species2vec"
date-released: 2026-05-23
keywords:
  - species embeddings
  - representation learning
  - biodiversity
  - GBIF
  - biogeography
  - fastText
abstract: >-
  species2vec learns distributed vector representations of species by
  treating geo-binned GBIF occurrence records as sentences and applying
  a fastText objective with atomic species tokens. Held-out evaluation
  (congener cosine gap, cross-genus sympatry AUC, neighbourhood
  self-rank) shows the embedding geometry encodes spatial range overlap
  rather than the morphology of binomial names.
